# college analyzes the relationship between students’ study hours and examination marks 
to understand how study time is associated with academic performance. The study hours are 
[2, 4, 6, 8, 10], and the corresponding marks are [35, 45, 60, 75, 85]. 
Write a Python program to calculate the sample covariance between study hours and marks, 
and to draw a scatter plot showing their relationship.



import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

x = [2,4,6,8,10]
y = [35,45,60,75,85]
print("Covariance:", np.cov(x,y)[0,1])
plt.scatter(x,y)
plt.show()
